  "worked_solution": "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{0}^{9}(2t-\\sqrt{t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={({t}^{2}-\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3/2})|}_{0}^{9} \\\\  & =[(9)^{2}-\\frac{2}{3}(9)^{3/2}]-[(0)^{2}-\\frac{2}{3}(0)^{3/2}] \\\\  & =81-18-0 \\\\  & =63.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total displacement between $t=0$ and $t=9$ is $63.$",
